---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { v } from '../lib/assetVersion';
---
<Base
  title="ADL Contrast Calculator | SpykeVision"
  description="Calculate and compare projector ADL contrast curves. Estimate from On/Off + ANSI, or plot known measurement points."
  active="calculator"
  alternate={true}
>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href={v("/css/adl-calc.css")} slot="head" />
  <script is:inline src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.0/dist/chart.umd.min.js" slot="head"></script>

  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="article-hero">
      <h1>ADL Contrast Calculator<span class="beta-tag">beta</span></h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-3);font-size:17px;margin-top:8px">Calculate an approximate ADL contrast curve from a few measurements, or plot known data points and compare multiple projectors.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="calc-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="calc-tab active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="estimate" onclick="switchTab('estimate')">Calculate ADL contrast</button>
      <button class="calc-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="manual" onclick="switchTab('manual')">Compare ADL contrast</button>
    </div>

    <!-- TAB 1: ESTIMATE -->
    <div class="calc-panel active" id="tab-estimate">
      <div class="prose" style="margin-bottom:20px">
        <p><strong>What this is.</strong> The On/Off contrast on a spec sheet is measured on a fully black frame — a situation that never occurs in real content. ADL contrast shows what happens once there is light on screen: 1% white, 5%, 50%. That curve, not the headline number, is what you actually watch.</p>
        <p>On/Off and ANSI are enough for an estimate. Add the 1% and 5% measurements and the curve gets sharper. Not sure where to start — hit <strong>Example</strong> for two real measured curves from the <a href="/reviews/titan-noir-max-cards/">Titan Noir Max In-Depth Review</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="estimateBlocks">
        <!-- filled by JS -->
      </div>
      <button class="add-btn" onclick="addEstimateBlock()">+ Add projector</button>

      <div class="calc-actions">
        <button class="btn" onclick="buildEstimateChart()">Calculate &amp; plot</button>
        <button class="btn-secondary" onclick="loadExample('estimate')">Example</button>
        <button class="btn-secondary" onclick="resetCalc('estimate')">Clear chart</button>
      </div>

      <div class="chart-wrap" id="estimateWrap">
        <div class="chart-toolbar">
          <span class="chart-title-mini">ADL contrast curve</span>
          <div class="chart-tools">
            <button class="chart-tool" data-scale="log" onclick="toggleScale('estimateChart', this)">Linear scale</button>
            <button class="chart-tool" data-xexpand="estimateChart" onclick="toggleXExpand('estimateChart', this)">Expand 0–5%</button>
            <button class="chart-tool" onclick="savePNG('estimateChart','spykevision-adl-estimate')">⬇ Save PNG</button>
            <button class="chart-tool" onclick="toggleExpand('estimateWrap','estimateChart', this)">⛶ Expand</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="chart-canvas-box"><canvas id="estimateChart"></canvas></div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:20px">
        <h3>How the estimate works</h3>
        <p>The curve is interpolated in log space directly through every value you enter (On/Off, 1% ADL, 5% ADL, ANSI) so it always passes exactly through your measured points. Gaps between points are interpolated and the tail beyond your last point is extrapolated from the local slope. The result is an estimate; real-world ADL behaviour can deviate, especially on projectors with aggressive dynamic iris.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- TAB 2: MANUAL -->
    <div class="calc-panel" id="tab-manual">
      <div class="prose" style="margin-bottom:20px">
        <p>Enter the exact measured contrast values for each ADL level. Leave fields blank if not measured; the chart will connect only the points you provide. Add multiple projectors to compare them side by side.</p>
        <p>Hit <strong>Example</strong> for three real measured curves from the <a href="/reviews/titan-noir-max-cards/">Titan Noir Max In-Depth Review</a> — zoom 1.0×, 1.5× and 2.0×.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="manualBlocks">
        <!-- filled by JS -->
      </div>
      <button class="add-btn" onclick="addManualBlock()">+ Add projector</button>

      <div class="calc-actions">
        <button class="btn" onclick="buildManualChart()">Plot</button>
        <button class="btn-secondary" onclick="loadExample('manual')">Example</button>
        <button class="btn-secondary" onclick="resetCalc('manual')">Clear chart</button>
      </div>

      <div class="chart-wrap" id="manualWrap">
        <div class="chart-toolbar">
          <span class="chart-title-mini">ADL contrast curve</span>
          <div class="chart-tools">
            <button class="chart-tool" data-scale="log" onclick="toggleScale('manualChart', this)">Linear scale</button>
            <button class="chart-tool" data-xexpand="manualChart" onclick="toggleXExpand('manualChart', this)">Expand 0–5%</button>
            <button class="chart-tool" onclick="savePNG('manualChart','spykevision-adl-measured')">⬇ Save PNG</button>
            <button class="chart-tool" onclick="toggleExpand('manualWrap','manualChart', this)">⛶ Expand</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="chart-canvas-box"><canvas id="manualChart"></canvas></div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </main>

  <script is:inline>
  window.ADL_LS_SUFFIX = '';
  window.ADL_I18N = {
    projPlaceholder: 'Projector name',
    projDefault:     'Projector',
    eg:              'e.g.',
    optional:        'Optional',
    onoffLabel:      'On/Off contrast',
    onoffHint:       'Full-field on/off (0% ADL)',
    ansiLabel:       'ANSI contrast',
    ansiHint:        '50% ADL checkerboard',
    apl1Label:       '1% ADL contrast',
    apl5Label:       '5% ADL contrast',
    contrastWord:    'contrast',
    estimatedSuffix: ' (estimated)',
    measuredSuffix:  ' (measured)',
    crossover:       'Crossover',
    xTitle:          '% of white (ADL)',
    yTitle:          'Contrast ratio',
    logScale:        'Log scale',
    linearScale:     'Linear scale',
    fullRange:       'Full range',
    expandLow:       'Expand 0–5%',
    expandBtn:       '⛶ Expand',
    closeBtn:        '✕ Close',
    plotFirst:       'Plot the chart first.',
    removeAria:      'Remove projector',
    demoNames:       ['Titan Noir Max · zoom 1.0×', 'Titan Noir Max · zoom 1.5×', 'Titan Noir Max · zoom 2.0×'],
    ansiWarn:        'ANSI contrast can’t be higher than On/Off contrast — check the values. This projector was skipped.'
  };
  </script>
  <script is:inline src={v("/js/adl-calc.js")}></script>
</Base>
